comparison between Edge (Normal Edge) and Conditional Edge in LangGraph.
========================================================================

| Feature                   | Edge (Normal Edge)                          | Conditional Edge                                                   |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Definition**            | Connects one node directly to another node. | Connects one node to multiple possible nodes based on a condition. |
| **Flow**                  | Fixed                                       | Dynamic                                                            |
| **Decision Making**       | ❌ No                                        | ✅ Yes                                                              |
| **Routing**               | Always follows the same path                | Chooses the next path based on logic                               |
| **Number of Next Nodes**  | One                                         | One of many possible nodes                                         |
| **Execution Path**        | Sequential                                  | Branching                                                          |
| **Method**                | `add_edge()`                                | `add_conditional_edges()`                                          |
| **Uses Router Function?** | ❌ No                                        | ✅ Yes                                                              |
| **Suitable For**          | Simple workflows                            | Intelligent AI agent routing                                       |
| **Complexity**            | Easy                                        | Moderate                                                           |
| **Example**               | Planner → Writer                            | Planner → Writer or Researcher or Coder                            |
| **Best Use Case**         | Fixed pipeline                              | Multi-Agent AI, Decision Making                                    |


==========

Example Flow
Edge (Normal Edge)
START
   |
Planner
   |
Researcher
   |
Writer
   |
END

Python:

graph.add_edge("planner", "researcher")
graph.add_edge("researcher", "writer")
graph.add_edge("writer", END)
Conditional Edge
                 Product
               /
Planner -------
               \
                \
                 FAQ
                  \
                   Payment

Python:

graph.add_conditional_edges(
    "planner",
    router,
    {
        "product": "product_agent",
        "faq": "faq_agent",
        "payment": "payment_agent",
    }
)

=========

Easy way to remember
Edge (Normal Edge) = One road → Always the same destination.
Conditional Edge = Road junction → Chooses the destination based on a condition or decision.

In LangGraph, add_edge() is used for fixed sequential workflows, while add_conditional_edges() is used to build intelligent, decision-driven Multi-Agent AI applications.

=========

| Use Edge (Normal Edge)   | Use Conditional Edge         |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------------- |
| Fixed workflow           | Dynamic workflow             |
| Sequential processing    | Decision-based routing       |
| One next step            | Multiple possible next steps |
| Simple automation        | Multi-Agent AI systems       |
| Data processing pipeline | AI Chatbots, RAG, Agentic AI |


